 - Storage Overlay — see the contents of every Ender Chest page and Backpack live, right alongside your open inventory
 - Bug Report — `/killer560 bugreport` builds one zip you can drag straight into Discord: your latest log, every one of the mod's config files, and a report of your mod/Minecraft/loader versions, which jar you are running, your OS, Java and memory, and every mod you have loaded. **Credentials are stripped before anything goes in.** Your session-login and account-proxy files are left out entirely rather than redacted, and in everything else any value whose name looks like a token, secret, password, auth, session or cookie is replaced with [redacted] - verified against a file containing six different fake credentials, all six removed, with keybinds and normal settings left untouched. Log lines are scrubbed the same way. It tells you where the zip is and opens the folder
 - Dungeon Sim — **work in progress, not part of a release yet.** A clear-practice dungeon you join from a Dungeon Sim button on the Multiplayer screen. It connects to nothing: it opens a flat local world this mod owns, and everything in it is client side. The button opens a chooser - load a previous run, create a new map, load a single room, or All Rooms (route practice, see Dungeon Sim Room Filters). The generator takes puzzle count and rooms-to-blood; the room picker has a search box and the sim's Filters panel (see Dungeon Sim Room Filters). Inside: etherwarp, Wither Impact, Tactical Insertion, Spirit Sceptre, Superboom, Dungeon Breaker and the Terminator (three arrows, and Salvation piercing five after three hits), all reimplemented locally, all swinging at Hypixel's 100 Attack Speed baseline. The Dungeon Breaker holds 20 charges, spends one per block and regains two a second, and every secret you get (chest, item, bat, essence) gives charges back, up to the 20: how many is the **Echoes of the Lost** slider in the mod menu's **Sim Settings** tab (the Wither Essence Shop perk of that name, whose five levels restore 1 to 5 charges per secret on hypixelskyblock.minecraft.wiki; 0 is the perk off, and it defaults to 5, the maxed perk) and it is saved across restarts. Mage is the only class, with the left-click beam, which has ZERO pierce - it kills the nearest thing you are looking at and nothing else. Mobs have 1 HP and never move, so a route is timed against the route rather than against where a mob wandered; starred ones carry the same name-tag stand Hypixel gives them, so Mob ESP and everything like it works unchanged. Fels sit as motionless skulls and wake into an upside-down enderman when you approach. Wither doors take a key, become barriers, then clear. One mimic per map. The sim used to outline every chest that could have been it, and that outline is gone: because every placed secret chest is a mimic candidate, it amounted to highlighting every secret on the floor whether or not Secret Waypoints was switched on. The sim has no highlighter of its own now - Secret Waypoints is the only thing that draws secrets in there, under exactly the setting that draws them on Hypixel. Score follows Catacombs: one point per crypt to five (counted when the crypt's undead dies, as Hypixel's "Crypts" line does; a prince's death also says "A Prince falls. +1 Bonus Score"), two for the mimic (a trapped chest, as on Hypixel: opening it puts a baby zombie there, and the point comes when that dies), Paul's EZPZ, and bats counting as secrets. `/speed <n>` sets speed on the Hypixel scale. `/simpuzzle <name>` builds a puzzle to drill. A five-second countdown holds you at the start of a full run. **State, 2026-10-01:** secrets come from the room database and land inside their rooms (asserted by a scenario that builds a floor and checks every chest). A Catacombs sidebar is put up on the sim's own integrated server, so the floor, the secret count, the keys and the room you are standing in read as they do on Hypixel. Rooms are rotated now: each capture's own quarter turn is recovered from its roof marker and its secrets, so a rotated room still puts its secrets in the right corner. **The eleven puzzle rooms are bound to their real geometry rather than to invented arenas** - the room's own levers, buttons, pads, lanterns, ice and boulders, found by scoring each puzzle's coordinates against the pasted blocks at all four rotations and refusing to arm a room they are not in. That means your own puzzle solvers and auto-puzzles work in there against the same data they use on Hypixel; `docs/SIM.md` records what each one was measured against. **Not done:** mobs (the captures hold no mob positions); a handful of rooms have imperfect captures (Balcony, Catwalk, Purple Flags); and none of it is tuned against a real floor yet
@@ -241,12 +241,8 @@ AP3 walks, aligns, leaps, uses items and times you through the F7/M7 Goldor phas
